n empire as well as suffering a  massive blow to their national prestige  it seemed a foregone conclusion that  hostilities would break out again so  both countries spent the following  decades in an arms race with each other  making huge strides forward in military  technology forging alliances and  crafting war plans formerly france and  germany were at peace but that didn't  stop networks of spies from operating in  both countries trying both to steal  military secrets and to protect their  own one of these spies was colonel  maximilian von schwarzkopfen  schwarzkopfen's official title was the  military attache to the german embassy  in paris but he had also been tasked by  kaiser wilhelm to collect intelligence  on french military defenses the special  interest was french artillery designs  which were at the cutting edge of  technology for the time schwarzkopfen  was a charming and sophisticated man  perfect for a diplomatic posting but he  was a remarkably careless secret agent  instead of destroying his correspondence  or locking up his important papers he  had a habit of halfheartedly tearing up  drafts or copies of letters and throwing  them in a waste basket unfortunately for  the german the embassy maid a local  parisian woman was secretly on the  payroll of the french  counterintelligence service which had  the cover name the bureau of statistics  the maid cleaned out the waste baskets  or swiped documents off of desks and  tables and then brought her findings to  her contact in the bureau who then  carefully taped the letters back  together in order to read them the  letters range from the banal to the  scandalous schwarzkopin was engaged in a  secret love affair with his counterpart  in the italian embassy alessandro  panziardi but one note known to history  as the border discovered in late  september 1894 was a letter from a spy  talking about several military documents  that had been delivered to the german  embassy along with the letter when the  document was delivered to the french  minister of war general auguste mercier  he was outraged there was a traitor  within the french army spying for the  hated germans the bureau of statistics  was given orders to find the traitor  whatever it took  on the morning of october 15 1894  captain alfred dreyfuss was summoned to  the office of the chief of the general  staff and less than an hour later was in  prison accused of betraying his country  to germany dreifus was completely  bewildered he had enjoyed a relatively  successful career in the army for the  last 15 years earning his way onto the  general staff as an artillery officer  from the very beginning he loudly  protested his innocence at every  opportunity so why was captain dreyfuss  suspected well the answer it seemed was  a simple one he was jewish jews living  in france had a considerably easier time  of things than their counterparts in  germany or russia where they were  regularly subjected to pogroms and were  largely segregated from society unlike  in those countries jews in france had  full citizenship and were active  participants in most of the nation's  professions but prejudice was  experiencing a resurgence in france in  the 1890s as anti-judaism hatred of the  jewish religion gave way to  anti-semitism hatred of the jews as a  race of people newspapers like libra  parole and lacroix routinely publish  pieces attacking jews as a malevolent  group accusing them of everything from  sacrificing christian children and blood  rituals to manipulating the continental  economy to enrich themselves and destroy  native businessmen all of french  society's ills could be blamed on the  jews and the thought of a jewish officer  betraying his country wasn't that  far-fetched to the many openly  anti-semitic members of the army  hierarchy in fact it was almost to be  expected it was in their sinister nature  according to them draper's court-martial  was held in closed session per the  army's request for reasons 