 picard wasn't going  to play ball with them they set out to  ruin first by transferring him to  tunisia and then by bringing him up on  trumped-up charges picard fought back  going first to sympathetic politicians  and then to the press with his  allegations at the same time matty  dreyfus mounted his own separate press  campaign insisting that there was  something wrong with his brother's  verdict more and more attention was  being brought what was now being called  the dreifus affair or simply le faire  public opinion was sharply divided on  one side were the dre facades who  supported reopening the case in light of  the new evidence and on the other were  the anti-dre facades who wanted the  conviction to be upheld anti-semitism  was central to the belief system of the  anti-dre facades stoked by virulent  rhetoric published in right-wing  newspapers the general staff leaned into  this hatred of the jews by openly  promoting the idea that they were  combating a vast jewish conspiracy a  syndicate who wanted to set dreyfus free  despite him being guilty of treason why  esterhazy's name began to circulate  among the dreyfussads as being the real  spy the general staff made the  incredible decision to protect him  sending a liaison officer to him with  advice to keep his mouth shut then when  the calls for action became too loud to  ignore they brought him to trial but his  court martial was a share his acquittal  was guaranteed before it even started so  to recap in order to hide the fact that  they had wrongfully convicted an  innocent man the army had deliberately  acquitted someone they knew to be guilty  for noted dre facade emile zola this was  the last straw zola was one of the most  celebrated authors of his day his novels  were widely read throughout europe  despite this he put his career and  reputation at risk to defend dreyfus  penning an open letter to the president  of france and publishing it in the  newspaper le aurore on january 13 1898.  under the headline jacuzz zola laid out  all of the accusations against the army  detailing for the first time to the  french public the depths of the  conspiracy to keep dreyfus in jail  jacuzz struck france like a bolt of  lightning people were shocked by the  dramatic reveal as well as the  subsequent trial of zola for libel when  zola's lawyer attempted to prove the  allegations laid out in the article zola  was ultimately convicted of libel and  sentenced to a year in jail the jury  unwilling to believe that the army one  of the most well-respected institutions  in the country would engage in such  conduct  alfred dreyfus had no idea at the battle  that was being waged on his behalf on  devil's island the prisoner was kept in  complete isolation his mail censored so  that details of his case never reached  him he lived in a tin roofed shack  surrounded by a stockade which did  nothing to keep out the oppressive heat  or the swarms of insects that attacked  him regularly his health steadily  deteriorated and his family were worried  that he would die over there before  being rehabilitated at this point it  seemed like the anti-dre facades had one  picar was discredited zola always a  convicted libeler esterhazy was quietly  retired from the army and left the  country and dreyfus was no closer to  retrial than he had been in 1894. but  the army's conspiracy was a house of  cards and one of their own was about to  inadvertently collapse the entire thing  the new minister of war gotta  forecavaniac was a fierce anti-dre  facade who took office with one goal in  mind to smash any doubt in the minds of  the french public about the guilt of  dreyfus to that end he ordered the  secret file containing more than 300  documents that were supposed to  definitively prove that dreyfus was a  spy to be opened and its contents  expertly evaluated this backfired  spectacularly on the army as it was soon  discovered that the only document in the  file that specifically mentioned dreyfus 