 headline jacuzz zola laid out  all of the accusations against the army  detailing for the first time to the  french public the depths of the  conspiracy to keep dreyfus in jail  jacuzz struck france like a bolt of  lightning people were shocked by the  dramatic reveal as well as the  subsequent trial of zola for libel when  zola's lawyer attempted to prove the  allegations laid out in the article zola  was ultimately convicted of libel and  sentenced to a year in jail the jury  unwilling to believe that the army one  of the most well-respected institutions  in the country would engage in such  conduct  alfred dreyfus had no idea at the battle  that was being waged on his behalf on  devil's island the prisoner was kept in  complete isolation his mail censored so  that details of his case never reached  him he lived in a tin roofed shack  surrounded by a stockade which did  nothing to keep out the oppressive heat  or the swarms of insects that attacked  him regularly his health steadily  deteriorated and his family were worried  that he would die over there before  being rehabilitated at this point it  seemed like the anti-dre facades had one  picar was discredited zola always a  convicted libeler esterhazy was quietly  retired from the army and left the  country and dreyfus was no closer to  retrial than he had been in 1894. but  the army's conspiracy was a house of  cards and one of their own was about to  inadvertently collapse the entire thing  the new minister of war gotta  forecavaniac was a fierce anti-dre  facade who took office with one goal in  mind to smash any doubt in the minds of  the french public about the guilt of  dreyfus to that end he ordered the  secret file containing more than 300  documents that were supposed to  definitively prove that dreyfus was a  spy to be opened and its contents  expertly evaluated this backfired  spectacularly on the army as it was soon  discovered that the only document in the  file that specifically mentioned dreyfus  by name a letter supposedly written by  the italian military attache was a  crudely constructed forgery to his  credit kavanagh didn't do what his  predecessors would have done that is  cover it all up instead he revealed the  forgery and conducted an investigation  into where it came from to the horror of  the anti-trade facades colonel uber  joseph orri who had been instrumental in  both the conviction of dreyfus and the  destruction of piccar was compelled to  confess to making the forgery on august  31 1898 a day after confessing to his  crime ori committed suicide by slitting  his throat with a razor the scandal  compelled the chief of general staff to  resign and revive the cause of the jury  facades over the course of the next year  three different prime ministers resigned  as their governing coalitions collapsed  and multiple officials quit their posts  the president of france died and his  successor was assaulted while attending  a horse race anti-semitic riots tore  through the country and there was an  attempted coup d'etat in february 1899  that failed after receiving no support  from the army it seemed like the  republic itself was under threat  attacked by a right-wing faction that  was both anti-semitic and anti-drafzard  to stop the chaos a new governing  coalition of republican defense was  formed in 1899 led by pierre walder  rousseau one of the first things on his  agenda settling the dravers affair once  and for all  [Music]  in june 1899 dravis conviction was set  aside by the supreme court and the man  at the center of a national fuhrer left  devil's island after four years of  torture to return to france he was to be  tried once again by military court  martial this time in the city of ren the  trial began on august 7 1899. many  people were shocked by the horrible  condition dreyfus was in his new uniform  flapped around his skeletal frame and he  looked like it aged 20 years the legal  drama that unfolded over the following  weeks was the 19th century equivalent of  the o.j simpson trial in terms of  international interest not only was all  of france riveted to the coverage of the  action in the newspapers but so was the  rest of europe and dispatches about each  day of the trial were sent across the  transatlantic telegraph cable to north  america as well it soon became apparent  to neutral observers just how flimsy the  prosecution's case against dreyfus  actually was the entire first trial had  revolved around draper's supposed  authorship of the border but now five  years later hardly anyone actually  believed that dreyfus had actually  written the letter the handwriting  expert whose testimony was crucial in  1894 was discredited after a number of  ridiculous comments including an  assertion that traifors had learned how  to forge his own handwriting esther hazy  who did not appear at the wren trial now  admit an impress interviews to write in  the note in question though he asserted  he only did to it the direction of  french intelligence and the fact that an  admitted forger colonel orri had handled  the document meant that it couldn't be  assured that it hadn't been tampered  with without the border row the rest of  the case against dreyfus seemed to fall  apart however the defense was her by  disorganization on the part of dreyfus's  attorneys it definitely didn't help that  one of the lawyers was shot in the back  by a would-be assassin on his way to  court a weak into the trial and in any  case dreyfus wasn't being tried by a  civilian court he was being tried by the  army and the army remained firmly behind  general mercier the war minister who had  overseen dreyfus's first conviction and  was just as sure of his guilt the second  time around when dreyfuss was convicted  again on september the 9th and sentenced  to 10 years imprisonment the dre facades  were shocked perhaps they shouldn't have  been at this point to the anti-dre  facades it didn't seem to matter whether  the man was actually guilty or not it  was all about the honor of the army  which apparently demanded that dreyfuss  be convicted regardless of the evidence  travis's second conviction sparked  international outcry france was accused  of being an arbitrary state contrary to  its supposed ideals even france's  closest ally russia ruled by one of  europe's last absolute monarchs thought  the verdict was wrongly decided there  was serious talk of boycotting the  world's fair to be held in paris the  next year prime minister waldek rousseau  had had enough he offered a compromise  instead of going through the ordeal of a  second retrial he offered dreyfus a  pardon that would free him immediately  unfortunately accepting a pardon also  requires a convicted person to accept  guilt for the crimes that they're being  pardoned for despite being initially  reluctant dreyfus ultimately accepted  leaving prison for the last time on  september 21 1899. it was a bitter pill  for the dre facades to swallow  especially when coupled with an amnesty  law passed in november that not only  cleared piccar and zola but also  prevented any of the conspirators that  had committed crimes to put dreifus in  prison from ever facing accountability  for it some of the more committed trey  facades who viewed the movement more as  one of social change than a campaign to  write the act of one injustice turned on  dreyfuss after he accepted the pardon  feeling like he had betrayed their cause  but it's hard to blame the man who after  all was innocent for not turning down a  chance to escape the hell he'd spent the  last five years in draper's hadn't  signed up for martyrdom all he wanted to  do was go home to his family most people  in his position would have probably done  the same thing  on july the 12th 1906 alfred dreyfus's  conviction at ren was officially quashed  by the supreme court this time there  would be no retrial dravis's 12-year  long legal ordeal was over by this time  the old leadership of the army had been  swept away replaced by a new generation  that wasn't so entrenched in their own  mystique to admit when a mistake had  been made organized anti-semitism had  largely fallen apart in france by 1902  and though it has never gone away it has  never again been embraced so openly by  the country not even when occupied by  the nazis during world war ii georges  pacar would eventually serve as minister  of war after being exonerated in the  amnesty of 1899. ferdinand esterhazy  would die in 1923 still in exile in  england under an assumed name alfred  dreyfuss was promoted to commandant the  day after his exoneration reflecting the  rank he would have had if his career  hadn't been disrupted he was also  decorated with the legion of honor the  only attempt at restitution that france  would ever give him the days of  multi-million euro settlements being  decades away not surprisingly drapers  didn't serve long in the army that had  betrayed him so viciously after being  rehabilitated retiring a year later he  returned to service during the first  world war seeing combat of adol among  other places he retired again in 1919 as  a colonel dreyfuss never really  recovered his health from his time spent  on devil's island his hair returned  permanently white and he was susceptible  to fevers and fatigue his sleep was  plagued by nightmares most likely caused  by untreated traumatic stress disorder  he was completely unable to separate  himself from the affair that had  consumed his life in 1908 while  attending the interment ceremony of emil  zola's remains in the pantheon in paris  anti-dre facade fnatic fired two shots  at him wounding him in the arm in the  last act of judicial bitterness the man  was acquitted after claiming he only  meant to wound dreyfus and wasn't trying  to kill him he died in 1935 quietly at  home surrounded by his family two days  later his funeral possession passed by  splendid formations of soldiers on its  way to his final resting place at  paris's montparnasse cemetery it was  bastille de france's national holiday a  celebration of the military glory of the  republic it was a fitting end for  someone who wanted nothing else but to  just be another french soldier before  his life was completely derailed by one  of the world's most famous miscarriages  of justice  [Music]  you
 

